WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:05.960
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this is going
to be my Mockingjay Review.

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:07.549
Hopefully you’ve had a chance to see it.

00:00:07.549 --> 00:00:11.720
Just in case I’m going to do a non-spoilery
part first and then I’ll get into favorite

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:13.230
moments with specific stuff.

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:18.000
I’m not quite as connected to the Hunger
Games books as much as Song of Ice and Fire,

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.279
I only read the first one.

00:00:21.279 --> 00:00:28.050
So when I saw Catching Fire and now this one
I didn’t know what was going to happen.

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:35.180
You can feel this giant shift in the tone
of the franchise within the first fifteen

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:40.010
minutes of the movie.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:44.520
The first two films were all about this big
epic event.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:45.520
The Games.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:49.129
And now that the line has been drawn in the
sand between these two big powers inside Panem

00:00:49.129 --> 00:00:54.179
it’s much more about the power of propaganda.

00:00:54.179 --> 00:00:57.309
Propaganda was a big part of the first two
movies, like when they made the tributes go

00:00:57.309 --> 00:00:58.960
on Ceasar’s show.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:05.040
It was very clear that all that was bullshit
and all the characters trying to survive it.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:07.190
Now Propaganda is the Games.

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:11.920
Or you could say it’s taken the role the
Games played in the story.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:16.050
A big call to action to the masses of Panem.

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:20.210
It’s just that now we get to hear the other
side’s story.

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:26.980
And they do have a lot of fun telling that
story inside the movie.

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:35.650
The circumstances are super depressing and
Katniss as a character is still very much

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:46.510
a reluctant non-traditional hero.

00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:56.710
But they’re still able to get some good
laughs in.

00:01:56.710 --> 00:02:00.200
It’s even funnier when you listen to what
the actors say about pranks they played on

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:01.780
each other while they were filming.

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:04.810
Liam Hemsworth said that anytime he’s ever
had a kissing scene with Jennifer Lawrence,

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:08.729
just to be funny she’s always eaten a ton
of garlic or something really gross right

00:02:08.729 --> 00:02:10.030
before they do it.

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:13.500
Elizabeth Banks as Effie also brings a lot
of humor to the story.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:17.319
Of all the films so far I enjoyed her the
most in Mockingjay.

00:02:17.319 --> 00:02:22.069
She’s always been the Clown but now she’s
like the Sad Clown, which for some reason

00:02:22.069 --> 00:02:23.280
seems funnier to me.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:26.500
I was never a giant fan of Woody Harrelson’s
Haymitch.

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:33.629
In real life he does share a lot of Haymitch’s
qualities but I always felt like he was miscast

00:02:33.629 --> 00:02:34.629
for the role.

00:02:34.629 --> 00:02:38.500
He has this strange acting style that feels
like it just doesn’t fit with a really serious

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:39.510
genre film like this.

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:41.890
I think he works better when he’s allowed
to be super crazy, like in Zombieland.

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:43.879
The Hunger Games movies feel like they take
themselves really seriously, which I don’t

00:02:43.879 --> 00:02:47.999
mind, but Mockingjay is by far the most serious
of them all, and Haymitch doesn’t feel like

00:02:47.999 --> 00:02:49.810
he belongs.

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:53.420
Julianne Moore and Philip Seymour Hoffman
were great together.

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:57.640
They’re both amazing character actors so
you instantly forget it’s them.

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:01.299
It’s always fun to watch actors disappear
into their characters.

00:03:01.299 --> 00:03:06.359
They made it a big point to state that they
didn’t use any CG to complete Hoffman’s

00:03:06.359 --> 00:03:07.359
scenes.

00:03:07.359 --> 00:03:15.810
He died before he’d finished his last few
scenes and they chose to just give those lines

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:16.810
to another character.

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:20.879
It’s not something you notice but the producers
made a big deal about explaining what they

00:03:20.879 --> 00:03:21.879
did.

00:03:21.879 --> 00:03:24.969
Just to address some of the criticism of breaking
the movie into two parts.

00:03:24.969 --> 00:03:28.670
I think the funniest comment I saw on twitter
was Duncan Jones, the director who’s doing

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:29.829
Warcraft right now.

00:03:29.829 --> 00:03:34.239
He said something like “The Only reason
to break the third movie in a trilogy into

00:03:34.239 --> 00:03:36.879
two parts, is because you want to buy a big
ass yacht.”

00:03:36.879 --> 00:03:43.150
I kind of agree, Mockingjay was written as
one book just like the other two.

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:45.160
If they could do the other two books in a
single film.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:47.640
They could have done Mockingjay in one film
too.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:51.730
If you really hate that people are doing this
with franchise movies now, you can blame Harry

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:53.269
Potter and Warner Brothers.

00:03:53.269 --> 00:04:03.249
They’re the first big franchise to do the
two part finale.

00:04:03.249 --> 00:04:05.420
Warner Brothers also did it again with the
Third Hobbit Movie.

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:10.000
The Hobbit was originally going to be directed
by Guillermo Del Toro and be just one film.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:15.120
But then Warner Brothers turned it into two
films, added a bunch of made up things that

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:16.120
weren’t in the book.

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:21.080
Then added a third film with even more made
up stuff.

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:29.450
And now studios can suddenly turn a 500 million
dollar profit into 2 or 3 billion dollars

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:31.410
over a 10 year period.

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:33.330
So this trend isn’t going away anytime soon.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:35.110
Disney is doing it with the Marvel films now.

00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:37.670
Avengers 3 is going to be broken into two
films.

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:43.560
Let’s all be honest though, we’ll still
spend the money to go see everything.

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:49.250
I’m just as big a part of the problem as
the studios because I support them financially.

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:50.250
Whatever.

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:53.280
Mockingjay is still a really fun ride, if
you haven’t read the books there are some

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:56.780
great big set pieces that will freak you out
in a really awesome way.

00:04:56.780 --> 00:04:59.080
The ending was a nice WTF.

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:02.860
And if you have read the book you’ll still
be crying your eyes out the whole time.

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:07.050
If you haven’t seen it yet it’s totally
worth the money to see it in a theater.

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:12.100
Here’s my big question for you guys, what
was your favorite moment and do you care that

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:14.870
they broke it into two parts to make more
money?

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:19.020
Now it’s time to get into spoilers, I’m
going to do my Top 5 moments so careful if

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:20.080
you haven’t seen it.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:21.990
Here we go.

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:24.790
Number 5 - President Snow Facts

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:28.290
Like I said, I hadn’t read the Catching
Fire or Mockingjay books, so there was a lot

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:31.320
I learned about President Snow when Finnick
went on the air.

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:33.310
When they were jamming the airwaves with spam.

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:36.030
They were spamming as a way to attack the
Capitol's defenses.

00:05:36.030 --> 00:05:38.220
Which was also a pretty cool trick.

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:41.410
Remember how I said propaganda was the core
of the film this time around.

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:47.050
The propaganda are the games now and there
are only two participants in the ring.

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:50.740
Finnick explained that he survived inside
the capitol by trading secrets, so it was

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:54.650
fun to listen to him spill his guts about
how President Snow rose to power.

00:05:54.650 --> 00:05:57.850
Like the fact that he uses the white roses
to cover the smell of blood in his mouth from

00:05:57.850 --> 00:06:03.900
wounds that will never heal.

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:07.910
Number 4 - Katniss In The Studio

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:11.350
The first time they try to make some fake
propaganda was like the first time the movie

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:12.580
let itself have fun.

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:15.500
The whole beginning is so depressing and serious.

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:20.690
All the Hunger Games movies in general begin
with the absence of action and even sound.

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:25.140
It’s one of the defining characteristics
of the franchise in that they begin on such

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:26.450
downer moments.

00:06:26.450 --> 00:06:29.210
So watching Katniss try to act was pretty
funny.

00:06:29.210 --> 00:06:31.570
And it brought Haymitch back into the story.

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:33.910
Even though he felt very out of place in district
13.

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:36.790
Number 3 - Jennifer Lawrence Singing The Hanging
Tree Song

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:40.440
I don’t think I’ve ever heard her sing
in any of her movies but I thought it was

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:41.830
beautifully melancholic.

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:44.830
You’re happy and sad at the same time.

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:51.031
The song is very appropriate to the story
of the movie, but just in general it was a

00:06:51.031 --> 00:06:54.650
great performance.

00:06:54.650 --> 00:06:57.530
Number 2 - Effie Trinket Hates District 13

00:06:57.530 --> 00:07:00.590
Elizabeth Banks was so much more fun this
time around.

00:07:00.590 --> 00:07:05.520
Sad Clown Effie Trinket has all this wit and
style and no one in District 13 gives a shit.

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:12.090
I was never a huge fan of fancy Effie during
the first two films, but she’s like the

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:16.790
pressure release valve for seriousness.

00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:18.270
Effie For the Win.

00:07:18.270 --> 00:07:24.420
Number 1 - Peeta Is Completely Nanners
Because I went into this not knowing the story

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:30.710
I thought President Snow was either going
to turn Peeta into one of those genetically

00:07:30.710 --> 00:07:32.440
altered dogs like in Catching Fire.

00:07:32.440 --> 00:07:38.590
I just remember that in one of the other books
the dead tributes get their DNA spliced with

00:07:38.590 --> 00:07:39.640
big freak attack dogs.

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:44.090
I thought that was what they were going to
find when they were traveling through the

00:07:44.090 --> 00:07:45.090
Tribute Center.

00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:50.550
The way they edited that whole sequence teased
a major reveal, so I was kind of dissapointed

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:51.880
when they just cut away.

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:56.520
It felt like it was building to something
else than them just being cut off from communications.

00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:59.070
The actual reveal, that Peeta was cranked
up on Tracker Jacker venom was a great ending

00:07:59.070 --> 00:08:00.070
though.

